WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.195
Your work has a home.

00:00:01.475 --> 00:00:03.053
Your screen does not have to.

00:00:03.333 --> 00:00:07.792
Meet Scheme: a small, self-hosted cockpit
for the computer that does the work.

00:00:08.342 --> 00:00:11.819
Your projects and terminal sessions stay
on your working computer.

00:00:12.099 --> 00:00:16.618
Open a browser on another desktop, a
laptop, or a phone, and reconnect through

00:00:16.618 --> 00:00:18.009
your private connection.

00:00:18.559 --> 00:00:19.561
Start with Shell.

00:00:19.841 --> 00:00:22.529
Open a terminal, run a command, and see
the result.

00:00:22.809 --> 00:00:26.543
This is the real application running on a
clean desktop machine.

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:29.077
Keep separate tasks in separate tabs.

00:00:29.357 --> 00:00:33.489
Choose Shell, Claude Code, Codex, or a
local model when those tools are

00:00:33.489 --> 00:00:34.071
installed.

00:00:34.351 --> 00:00:37.103
Your own accounts and hardware power the
tools you choose.

00:00:37.653 --> 00:00:41.995
Find a session, return to its project, and
follow the activity your tools

00:00:41.995 --> 00:00:42.411
report.

00:00:42.691 --> 00:00:46.589
Missing information stays unknown, so the
dashboard does not pretend to know

00:00:46.589 --> 00:00:47.512
more than it does.

00:00:48.062 --> 00:00:50.558
Close the browser and let the host keep
working.

00:00:50.838 --> 00:00:52.417
Come back to the same terminal.

00:00:52.697 --> 00:00:56.746
We tested that on two independent desktop
machines, including a job that

00:00:56.746 --> 00:00:58.883
finished while the browser was closed.

00:00:59.433 --> 00:01:00.479
Change the theme.

00:01:00.759 --> 00:01:02.188
Make room for the terminal.

00:01:02.468 --> 00:01:05.135
Use the smaller-screen controls when space
is tight.

00:01:05.415 --> 00:01:08.167
The same workspace adapts to the screen in
front of you.

00:01:08.717 --> 00:01:11.149
Keep the working computer powered on and
awake.

00:01:11.429 --> 00:01:15.354
A reboot ends running processes, even when
saved tabs reopen.

00:01:15.634 --> 00:01:19.559
A private connection protects access to
the computer that holds your work.

00:01:20.109 --> 00:01:20.856
Scheme.

00:01:21.136 --> 00:01:23.077
Your working computer, from any screen.

00:01:23.357 --> 00:01:27.411
Open the setup guide, watch the full
walkthrough, and try your first terminal.
